! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F208D "INDICATOR TESTS"
! for ADD DOUBLE, sub-tests D1-D6 (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf
! pp.98-99, octal 015145.00-015167.40, where F208D7 / SAP9G begins):
! the Lost Carry and Lost Significance indicators.
!
! Each sub-test clears the indicator it is about to test with the
! branch-and-zero form (BLCZ / BLSZ branch over the next half-word AND
! zero the indicator), runs one D+, then asks with BZLC/BLC or
! BZLS/BLS whether it came on.
!
!   D1  LC on:  FPK21 + FPK21 unnormalized. Both fractions have the
!       top bit set, so the sum carries out of bit 12 and the carry is
!       lost -- there is no post-shift to catch it.
!   D2  LC off: the same addition NORMALIZED. The normalizing right
!       shift keeps the carry, so LC stays off. D1 against D2 is the
!       whole point: same operands, one modifier apart.
!   D3  LS on:  an exact cancellation. FPK31 with FPK33's fraction in
!       its low half, minus FPK33, is a zero 96-bit result fraction
!       while NEITHER operand is zero.
!   D4  LS off: FPK0 + FPK0. The result fraction is zero too, but so
!       are both operands, and p.96 sets LS only "when at least one
!       operand is non-zero".  D3 against D4 is that clause.
!   D5  LS on:  FPK21 with FPK41's fraction, plus FPK42.
!   D6  LS off: the listing's note is "result contains propagated
!       EF+1". FK35 is flagged and FK32 is in the N range, so this
!       goes down the FLAGGED path, which returns one operand whole
!       rather than adding -- and the operand it returns has a zero
!       fraction. LS must still stay off, because nothing was lost:
!       no addition happened. That is the one sub-test here that says
!       anything about the flagged path's indicators.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool pp.176-177. D7-D11, "TEST EXPONENT RANGE INDICATORS", are not
! transcribed here; PASS sits exactly where SAP9G begins.
!
! Note on lengths: the branch-on-INDICATOR ops are half-word (format
! 2), unlike the branch-on-BIT ops BB/BZB, which are full-word. That
! is what makes D1 five half-words rather than six.
!
! Instructions: B, BLCZ/BZLC/BLC, BLSZ/BZLS/BLS, DL(U), C0011 into the
! accumulator at offset 20, D+(U)/D+(N)/D-(U), SIC.
! verify_fp_arith_f208d1_6_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool pp.176-177) --

        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22032.0
FPK21   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031177777777777777767
        SLC, (8)22044.0
FPK31   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22046.0
FPK33   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777740
        SLC, (8)22056.0
FPK41   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001040000000000000000
FPK42   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001460000000000000000
        SLC, (8)22202.0
FK32    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0027125252525252525000
        SLC, (8)22205.0
FK35    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777400000000000000000

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15145.0
SAP9F   BLCZ, $+.32            ! F208D1: test LC ind on, unnormalized
        DL(U), FPK21
        D+(U), FPK21
        SIC, SEN
        BZLC, SERS             ! error if LC not on
        B, $+.32               ! F208D2: test LC ind off, normalized
        BLCZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK21
        D+(N), FPK21
        SIC, SEN
        BLC, SERS              ! error if LC on
        B, $+.32               ! F208D3: test LS ind, on condition
        BLSZ, $+.32
        DL(U), FPK31
        C0011(BU,48), FPK33+.12, 20
        D-(U), FPK33           ! zero result fraction, neither operand zero
        SIC, SEN
        BZLS, SERS             ! error if LS not on
        BLSZ, $+.32            ! F208D4: test LS ind off
        DL(U), FPK0
        D+(U), FPK0            ! zero result fraction, both operands zero
        SIC, SEN
        BLS, SERS              ! error if LS on
        BLSZ, $+.32            ! F208D5: test LS ind on
        DL(U), FPK21
        C0011(BU,48), FPK41+.12, 20
        D+(U), FPK42
        SIC, SEN
        BZLS, SERS             ! error if LS ind off
        B, $+.32               ! F208D6: test LS ind, off condition
        BLSZ, $+.32            ! result contains propagated EF+1
        DL(U), FK35
        D+(U), FK32
        SIC, SEN
        BLS, SERS              ! error if LS on
PASS    BEW, $                 ! 015167.40: where F208D7 / SAP9G begins
        END, SAP9F
